Subject: [PATCH] avfoundation: reuse frame buffers and streamline subtitle compositing

Keep frame-buffer allocation bounded while waiting for reusable buffers before
presentation deadlines, with a separate reserve for paused frame replacement.
Reuse pool allocation attributes, software-upload color metadata, and subtitle
color-conversion matrices instead of recreating them for each frame.

Composite subtitles in place on owned software-upload buffers, limit float
subtitle images to visible bounds, and skip transparent pixels and redundant
color conversions. Avoid unnecessary bitmap contexts, attachment copies, and
row-by-row copies when strides match. Track pixel transformations explicitly
so in-place overlays invalidate dynamic HDR metadata correctly.

